Bugfix: Reject invalid exclude patterns with a syntax error after `*`

Exclude and include patterns such as `x[a]*[` passed the pattern validation
although they are malformed. The backup then printed a syntax error for each
path the pattern partly matched, backed those paths up anyway and exited with
status 0. Restic now rejects such patterns up front with an "invalid pattern(s)
provided" error.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22173
